      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2015 The Author(s).",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "Label": "UNLABELLED",
            "content": "The causes of heel cord pain after repair of acute rupture of the Achilles tendon are unclear. The proposed etiologies include nonabsorbable suture granuloma formation, alteration of the pain receptors threshold in the tendon, and distension of the paratenon by the hypertrophied tendon, underlying tendinopathy, postrepair neovascularization, and peritendinous fibrous adhesion. We present an endoscopic technique of adhesiolysis of the Achilles tendon to deal with the various possible causes of postrepair heel cord pain."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "LEVELS OF EVIDENCE",
            "content": "Therapeutic, Level 4: Case report."
          }
        ]
      },
